From: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] b43: wait for the N-PHY TX I/Q LO calibration to finish

b43_nphy_cal_tx_iq_lo() writes a calibration command to IQLOCAL_CMD and
then polls the same register, meaning to wait until the engine is done
before reading the results out of the IQLOCAL table. The test is
inverted:

	for (i = 0; i < 2000; i++) {
		tmp = b43_phy_read(dev, B43_NPHY_IQLOCAL_CMD);
		if (tmp & 0xC000)
			break;
		udelay(10);
	}

Bits 15 and 14 are set while the calibration runs, so the loop leaves on
its first read, roughly ten microseconds after the command was issued.
The driver then reads offsets 96 and up and stores them as the best
coefficients, and repeats that for all twelve commands: what it stores
is whatever the table held before the engine wrote to it.

The reference spins the other way, waiting for the two bits to clear:

	write_phy_reg(pi, 0xc0, cal_cmd);
	SPINWAIT(((read_phy_reg(pi, 0xc0) & 0xc000) != 0), 20000);

SPINWAIT() loops while its expression is true, and the budget is the
same one this loop already has, 20000 us in steps of 10.

An MMIO capture of wl 6.30.102.7 on a BCM6362 (N-PHY rev 8, radio 2057
rev 8) issues the same twelve commands in the same order and reads
IQLOCAL_CMD 455 times between the first and the last. Before this change
the driver reads it 12 times, once per command; after it, 455, and the
matched operations over the calibration rise from 741 of 1570 to 1195.

This is not specific to radio 2057 rev 8: the loop is shared by every
N-PHY the driver drives, so it is deliberately not gated.

Verified: records #8637-#10697, between the two writes of
"PHY.WR   addr=0x00c2"
Link: https://github.com/aleferri/b43-6362-wip/blob/d2c490d/router-data/dsl-3580l/opinit-ch1-ch6-bw20.decoded
Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmsmac/phy/phy_n.c?id=848acc8ffe1b#n25881
Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/include/brcmu_utils.h?id=848acc8ffe1b#n16

Signed-off-by: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
---
index 22359bd9d..f3cdbdd8f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
@@ -5479,7 +5479,7 @@ static int b43_nphy_cal_tx_iq_lo(struct b43_wldev *dev,
 			b43_phy_write(dev, B43_NPHY_IQLOCAL_CMD, cmd);
 			for (i = 0; i < 2000; i++) {
 				tmp = b43_phy_read(dev, B43_NPHY_IQLOCAL_CMD);
-				if (tmp & 0xC000)
+				if (!(tmp & 0xC000))
 					break;
 				udelay(10);
 			}
